Use one name rule for the installed background image

The extension helper scanned the whole path for the last dot, so a
folder name with a dot became the extension. An empty file selection
resolved to the save folder, and the installer then wrote a
configuration value that names no file. The remover dropped the
extension that the installer appends, so every copied image stayed in
the configuration folder.

Take the extension from the file name alone, install only from a real
file, and remove every name that the installer can write. No string of
the dialog changes, and a saved configuration reads unchanged.

The change sits on the branch work/image-dialog of the local tree, as commit 5 of 5.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

